+- **Main's M68 and M69, on top of T7b part 1 as landed:** each run has its own `/tmp`, `/var/tmp` and `/dev/shm` (a mount
+  namespace, the run's folder bound at `/mnt`, a fresh tmpfs over each), so no run leaves a file for another; the probe
+  accepts a namespace in which no interface but the loopback is up (a kernel with tunnel modules shows them down), and
+  refuses a wrap whose `/tmp` is shared; the guard refuses `exec`, `eval`, `compile` and `__import__` only as bare names or
+  as attributes of `builtins`, so `re.compile` passes, and its docstring says it sees only what is written plainly;
+  discovery passes over main's own card carried by a seat's branch (the same path and blob as on main).
+- **Main's M70:** the run is in its own IPC and PID namespaces as well, and every world-writable directory the runner finds
+  (`/run/lock`, `/dev/mqueue` and any other) is covered by a fresh tmpfs; every process of nobody is killed before and
+  after each run, under a lock that keeps sandboxed runs one at a time on a machine, and a run that leaves one that
+  cannot be killed is HEAVY. The probe reports, as JSON, its user and groups,
+  a write outside every tmpfs refused for want of permission only, and every directory it can write, searched over the
+  whole filesystem; a wrap that keeps root, or misses a world-writable directory, is refused. Discovery also passes over
+  main's card as it stood at the merge-base of a seat's branch and main. The guard follows `builtins` through its aliases
+  and refuses `exec`, `eval`, `compile` and `__import__` imported from it.
